WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.021
Week 33: History, Society, and Multiple Perspectives. summarize a historical development distinguish fact from interpretation compare perspectives

2
00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:19.913
Cultural lens. Colonization, independence, migration, dictatorship, democracy, identity, and memory require country-specific framing.

3
00:00:19.913 --> 00:00:32.006
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:43.800
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:52.842
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:52.842 --> 00:01:26.460
Model language. La colonización requiere un marco específico. — Colonization requires specific framing. Lo mismo ocurre con la independencia. — The same is true of independence. La dictadura y la democracia se viven distinto según el país. — Dictatorship and democracy are experienced differently by country. La identidad no se puede generalizar. — Identity cannot be generalized. Cada país concreto tiene su propia historia. — Each specific country has its own history.

7
00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:36.358
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
